.TH FILMCRAFT-CLI 1 "November 2026" "FilmCraft 0.20.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
filmcraft\-cli \- FilmCraft from the command line: command runner, exporter and MCP server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B filmcraft\-cli
.RI [ options ]
.I subcommand
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B filmcraft\-cli
runs FilmCraft's editor commands without a window, in a headless engine, or against a running FilmCraft window with
.BR \-\-bridge .
It needs no windowing system and no GPU.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.BI "exec " "id " [ key=value " ...]"
Run one command and print its result as JSON. The parameters can also be given as one JSON object.
.TP
.BR run " \fIscript.jsonl\fR | \-"
Run commands, one JSON object with an
.I id
and
.I params
per line, in order.
.TP
.BR commands " [\fIfilter\fR] [\-\-json]"
List the commands.
.TP
.BI describe " id"
Print one command as JSON.
.TP
.BR inspect " [project|sequence]"
Print the project tree or the active sequence as JSON.
.TP
.BI import " file ..."
Import media into the project.
.TP
.BI export " out " [ options ]
Export the active sequence and wait for it to finish, with an export preset (\fBexport \-\-list\-presets\fR) or a
format guessed from the extension.
.TP
.B render
Render one Program frame to PNG (\fB\-\-seconds\fR \fIS\fR \fB\-\-out\fR \fIf.png\fR).
.TP
.BI probe " media"
Print information about a media file as JSON.
.TP
.B mcp
Run an MCP server on standard input and output, so that an AI agent can drive the editor engine, headless or
with
.B \-\-bridge
attached to a running window.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-project " p.fcproj"
Open this project first (headless).
.TP
.B \-\-demo
Open the built-in demo project (headless).
.TP
.B \-\-save
Save the project back to
.B \-\-project
when done.
.TP
.BI \-\-save\-as " p.fcproj"
Save the project to this path when done.
.TP
.BI \-\-bridge " 127.0.0.1:PORT"
Send commands to the running app (started with
.BR "filmcraft \-\-control PORT" ).
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.PP
.B filmcraft\-cli help
prints the full usage.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 when a command failed, or when an export or render drew offline media without
.BR \-\-allow\-offline ;
2 on a usage error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR filmcraft (1)
.PP
https://getartcraft.com/apps/filmcraft
